---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "@/components/PageHeader.astro";
import CtaBand from "@/components/CtaBand.astro";
import ReviewCard from "@/components/ReviewCard.astro";
import holly from "@/assets/holly.jpg";

import { site } from "@/data/site";
import { publishedReviews } from "@/data/reviews";

const years = new Date().getFullYear() - site.foundedYear;

/**
 * The trust page. For a service where a stranger holds your house key, this is
 * usually the second page someone opens, and it is where the decision is
 * actually made.
 */
const title = `About Holly Rising | Cat Sitter in Boca Raton Since ${site.foundedYear}`;
const description = `Holly Rising has been caring for cats in West Boca Raton, Delray Beach and Deerfield Beach since ${site.foundedYear}. One sitter, cats only, in your own home. ${site.reviews.rating}★ across ${site.reviews.count} Google reviews.`;

const longTenure = publishedReviews.filter((r) => r.tenure).slice(0, 2);
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title="I’m Holly, and I’ve been doing this a long time"
    lead={`I started Best In Boca Pet Sitters in ${site.foundedYear}. ${years} years later I’m still the one who turns up at your door.`}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about__grid">
      <div class="about__media">
        <Image
          src={holly}
          alt="Holly Rising, owner of Best In Boca Pet Sitters, holding a cat"
          widths={[420, 640, 900]}
          sizes="(min-width: 64em) 28vw, 92vw"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          class="about__img"
        />

        <aside class="about__facts">
          <h2 class="about__facts-title">At a glance</h2>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Started</dt><dd>{site.foundedYear}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Specialty</dt><dd>Indoor cats, in their own home</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Areas</dt><dd>{site.serviceAreas.join(", ")}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Reviews</dt><dd>{site.reviews.rating}★ from {site.reviews.count} on Google</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Paperwork</dt><dd>Service agreement &amp; vet release</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div class="about__copy prose">
        <h2>Why cats only</h2>
        <p>
          For years I looked after everything &mdash; dogs, cats, the lot. These
          days I take cats and nothing else, and it&rsquo;s made me much better
          at the job.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cats are easy to get wrong. People assume they&rsquo;re fine on their
          own for a few days, and mostly they are, right up until they
          aren&rsquo;t. A cat who stops eating on day two, a litter box that
          tells you something&rsquo;s wrong, the one who hides for the first
          three visits and then decides you&rsquo;re acceptable &mdash; you only
          learn to read that by doing it several thousand times. Narrowing down
          to cats means every visit I make builds on the last one.
        </p>

        <h2>Why I don&rsquo;t board</h2>
        <p>
          I don&rsquo;t take cats into my home, and I wouldn&rsquo;t want to.
          Cats are territorial. Nearly all of them do better in their own house,
          with their own smells and their own windows and the same spot on the
          sofa, than in a strange place surrounded by strange animals. They love
          their own home best.
        </p>
        <p>
          There&rsquo;s a practical benefit too: because I&rsquo;m coming to your
          house anyway, you also get someone walking through it while
          you&rsquo;re away. I&rsquo;ll bring in the mail so it isn&rsquo;t
          piling up in view, water the plants, and move the lights and blinds
          around so the place looks lived-in. Over twenty years I&rsquo;ve found
          leaks, failed air conditioning, and a few things a burglar would have
          been glad to find first.
        </p>

        <h2>The same person, every time</h2>
        <p>
          There&rsquo;s no rota here and no app assigning you whoever&rsquo;s
          available. You meet me, you book me, and I&rsquo;m the one your cat
          sees. Some of my clients have been with me for ten years. Some of the
          cats I&rsquo;ve known since they were kittens.
        </p>
        <p>
          That&rsquo;s the part the big platforms can&rsquo;t do, and
          it&rsquo;s the part that matters when your cat is shy, or elderly, or
          takes three visits to come out from under the bed.
        </p>

        <h2>What I don&rsquo;t do</h2>
        <p>
          I&rsquo;d rather be straight with you now than at your front door. I
          don&rsquo;t administer medication of any kind. I don&rsquo;t care for
          outdoor cats, because I can&rsquo;t do the job properly if I
          can&rsquo;t reliably find them. And I don&rsquo;t take on cats who are
          seriously ill or near the end of their lives &mdash; they deserve
          someone with medical training, and pretending otherwise
          wouldn&rsquo;t be fair to them.
        </p>
        <p>
          If any of that rules me out, please still call. I know the people in
          this area and I&rsquo;m glad to point you toward the right kind of
          help.
        </p>

        <h2>Before your first visit</h2>
        <p>
          We&rsquo;ll meet at your house, free of charge, so you can see how I
          am with your cat and I can learn their routine. We&rsquo;ll sign a
          service agreement and a veterinary release &mdash; the release is what
          lets me get your cat to a vet quickly if it&rsquo;s ever needed,
          rather than waiting to track you down while you&rsquo;re on a plane.
        </p>
        <p>
          It takes about twenty minutes, and in my experience it&rsquo;s the
          twenty minutes that lets everyone stop worrying.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="about__reviews-title">People who&rsquo;ve stayed a while</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2">
        {longTenure.map((review) => <ReviewCard review={review} truncate />)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Come and meet me"
    body="The first visit is free and nothing’s booked until we’ve met. Call, or send a few details and I’ll be in touch."
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sp-7);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 64em) {
    .about__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 0.75fr 1.25fr;
      gap: var(--sp-8);
    }

    .about__media {
      position: sticky;
      top: 6rem;
    }
  }

  /* Same 4:5 crop as the home page — see the note there. */
  .about__img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 22%;
    border-radius: var(--r-xl);
  }

  .about__facts {
    margin-top: var(--sp-5);
    padding: var(--sp-5);
    background-color: var(--c-blush-tint);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-blush-deep);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
  }

  .about__facts-title {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--c-sage-text);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .about__facts dl {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
  }

  .about__facts dt {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--c-ink-muted);
  }

  .about__facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--c-plum);
  }

  .about__copy p {
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .about__reviews-title {
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-6);
  }
</style>
